    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full test suite consists of `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are an abstract base and a helper), and all 3 tests are green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store numbers in E.164 form. Three files changed:\n\n**`Owner.java`** (entity validation) \u2014 replaced the old 10-digit constraints (`@Digits` + `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")`) with an E.164 pattern `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, so persistence accepts the normalized value.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 rewrote `normalizeTelephone` to produce E.164:\n- strips spaces, dashes and brackets;\n- keeps a leading `+` and country code when present;\n- otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits;\n- requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, returning `null` (\u2192 HTTP 400) otherwise.\n\n`isTelephoneInUse` now compares E.164 values (normalizing each existing owner's stored number before comparison, which is idempotent for already-E.164 values).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` field description and example to document the new E.164 normalization.\n\nVerified against the spec's cases: `'0412 345 678'` \u2192 `'+61412345678'`, `'+64 21 123 456'` \u2192 `'+6421123456'`, and `'12'` \u2192 rejected with 400.",
